\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Experimental architecture. One data spine (left) feeds two model arms that differ in exactly one respect: whether they consume training data. Both answer the \emph  {same} items---so every encoder--LLM comparison is paired item-for-item---and both pass through one strict scoring spine (right). The band beneath is the study's independent variable: the distribution shift between what a model was fitted on and what it is scored on.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
